2025-09-05 01:20:48,359 - evaluation_logger_Attraction-6 - INFO - Final Response: Here are the top trending things to do in Cambridge right now (family‑friendly picks):

- Small-Group Punting Tour (guided on the River Cam)
  - From about $23.40, free cancellation. Relaxing, classic Cambridge experience; easy with kids.

- 24-hour Hop-on, Hop-off Bus Tour
  - From about $22.10, free cancellation. See highlights at your own pace; stroller-friendly.

- Alumni-Led Walking Tour with optional King’s College entry
  - From about $25.98, free cancellation. Student/alumni guides with insider stories; option to add King’s College/Chapel.

- Cambridge University Walking Tour
  - From about $32.49, free cancellation. Covers iconic colleges and university history.

- “Creepy Cambridge” Ghost Walk
  - From about $24.68, free cancellation. Fun storytelling; best for tweens/teens.

Family-friendly must-see sights to add:
- King’s College Chapel and the Backs (classic views)
- Fitzwilliam Museum (great collections; typically free entry)
- Cambridge University Botanic Garden
- Market Square and nearby streets for snacks and souvenirs
- Sedgwick Museum of Earth Sciences (dinosaurs, fossils)
- The Polar Museum (Scott Polar Research Institute)

Tips:
- Punting is most popular on weekends/afternoons—consider morning slots to avoid crowds.
- Hop-on bus + short walking tour makes an easy day with kids.
- Check college/chapel opening times (events can limit access).

Want me to check real-time availability and prices for your dates? Share:
- Travel dates and preferred times
- Number of adults and kids (with ages)
- Interests (boats, museums, walking, spooky fun)
